The Hopper and Hopper (G) LoRA adapter weights are offered for research and demo use only, not for
commercial use, because their training data included passages from RACE (via the cais/mmlu
auxiliary set). RACE's authors release it for non-commercial research only, and its terms extend to
derived data. See MODEL_CARD.md.

The Hopper 12B (trained) LoRA adapter (HopitAI/hopper, branch hopper-12b) and its readout map
(hopper_decisions/maps/hopper-12b-trained-readout.json) are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Their training data did not include RACE.

Base model
  The adapter is trained on, and only runs with, Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B, revision 851bf6e806efd8d0a36b00ddf55e13ccb7b8cd0a),
  Copyright Alibaba Cloud, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B/blob/main/LICENSE
  The base model's weights are not included here; they are downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub.

Hopper 12B base model
  `hopper-serve --base-loader gemma-4-12b-it` runs google/gemma-4-12B-it
  (https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-12B-it, revision 707f0a3b8a3c7ad586ed01e27eafbad8a27dd0f7),
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, subject to Gemma's upstream terms and
  prohibited-use policy. Its weights are not included here; they are downloaded from the Hugging
  Face Hub.

Optional embedding model
  `hopper-serve --shortlist embedding` (off by default) uses Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B, revision 97b0c614be4d77ee51c0cef4e5f07c00f9eb65b3),
  Copyright Alibaba Cloud, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its weights are not
  included here; they are downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub only when that option is used.

Prompt layout
  The JSON prompt layout in hopper_decisions/prompt.py re-implements the layout of SemIf's
  core.direct_messages (https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TheoLeeCJ).
  No SemIf code is copied.

JevBench
  hopper_decisions/speed.py restates the Speed formula of JevBench
  (https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Florian Standhartinger
  and contributors). No JevBench item is included in this repository or in the training data.

Training data
  The Hopper adapter's training data includes examples derived from the public datasets listed in
  MODEL_CARD.md ("Training data"), each used under its own licence as stated there.
  The Hopper 12B (trained) adapter was trained on rows converted (modified) from SNLI, ARC,
  HotpotQA and SQuAD2 (CC BY-SA 4.0); CUAD, BANKING77, QASC and xLAM/APIGen (CC BY 4.0; APIGen:
  Liu et al., 2024, arXiv:2406.18518); CLINC150 (CC BY 3.0); MAMS, ESCI, the Glaive-v2 and
  Hermes-FC schemas, and ToolACE (Apache-2.0); CommonsenseQA (MIT); and API-Bank training data
  (MIT Hub mirror; upstream Apache-2.0 notice conditions also followed). Links and credits are in
  README.md ("Hopper 12B (trained)"). The adapter is distributed without its training data.
